      "content": "While rest, good nutrition, and over-the-counter remedies like electrolytes and magnesium can sometimes help replenish energy levels and improve overall well-being, your persistent symptoms shouldn't be ignored. They could indicate more serious cardiovascular or respiratory issues, especially with the heavy feeling in the chest when moving around. Although you might feel pressed for time and financial resources, not addressing your symptoms immediately could lead to more serious issues in the future. Consider reaching out to a community health clinic or telehealth service, which may offer affordable InsightDiagnosis for a shift, or perhaps even free or sliding-scale services. Your health is care provider in this situation. Speaking with a health professional about your symptoms can provide peace of mind and guidance on the best course of action, which may prevent more significant health problems later on. Giving your body the time it needs to recover, even with the challenges you're facing, is crucial. Your health should always be a priority, and there are often resources available that can provide the care you need even with budget and time constraints. Keep in mind that delaying medical care can result in higher costs and worse health outcomes in the long run. Health and safety come first.",
